# Cloudflare Pages headers for QueryDrop.
# Cross-Origin Isolation required for DuckDB-WASM high-perf mode
# (SharedArrayBuffer + pthreads). COEP: credentialless keeps the isolation
# while allowing no-cors third-party subresources (Google AdSense iframes)
# that don't send CORP headers — require-corp would block ads outright.
# https://web.dev/articles/coop-coep

# Cross-Origin Isolation for the entire app
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://plausible.io https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.googleadservices.com https://*.google.com https://*.gstatic.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://*.gstatic.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://*.google.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.googleadservices.com https://*.gstatic.com; frame-src https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://*.doubleclick.net; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-ancestors 'none'

# DuckDB WASM bundles are served from the jsdelivr CDN (see src/lib/duckdb/client.ts)
# — Cloudflare Pages rejects files over 25MB, and the wasm binaries are 36-41MB.

# Long-cache hashed assets (Astro auto-names these with content hashes)
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Security headers (applies to all routes)
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
